{"availability":"available","full":"damonko1/demoPrediction","name":"demoPrediction","description":"Interactive election scenario simulator for President, House, and Senate — transparent assumptions, live maps, no signup.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-29T20:19:22Z","updated":"2026-08-29T17:20:43Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://damonko1.github.io/demoPrediction/","topics":["civic-tech","data-visualization","election-simulator","nextjs","react","typescript"],"demo":"https://damonko1.github.io/demoPrediction/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.661Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.661Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.661Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.661Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive, browser-based lab for exploring how election assumptions can change the presidential, House, and Senate map.","Election Scenario Playground turns national swing and local race assumptions into immediate visual results. The default experience focuses on the 2026 House midterms, with Senate and historical presidential workspaces alongside it. Start from a sourced historical baseline, apply a preset or build a custom scenario, then inspect which states and seats move—and why. Scenarios are encoded in the URL, so an interesting map can be shared without creating an account.","This is an educational scenario simulator, not a polling average, election forecast, or statement about voter behavior. Presets and demographic weights are transparent stress-test assumptions. Read the data accuracy policy before interpreting or extending the model."],"features":["Three connected workspaces: Explore House and Senate midterm scenarios, with historical presidential replay available for context.","Historical replay: Use calculation-ready state presidential baselines for every election from 2000 through 2024.","Interactive election maps: Inspect all 538 electoral votes, 435 voting House districts, and 100 Senate seats with margin-based color intensity.","Real-time scenario controls: Adjust national swing and demographic-style assumptions and see the map, counters, summaries, and pressure points update immediately.","One-click stress tests: Try youth-turnout, suburban-shift, rural-surge, low-turnout, and popular-vote/Electoral College split scenarios."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damonko1/demoPrediction/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"000102e4b0eefd3f5829faea3ed868817a981696e4ff408f8d78ff0ccac4762c","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.793Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.793Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interactive, browser-based lab for exploring how election assumptions can change the presidential, House, and Senate map.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damonko1/demoPrediction/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"000102e4b0eefd3f5829faea3ed868817a981696e4ff408f8d78ff0ccac4762c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damonko1/demoPrediction/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.794Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-29T17:20:43Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damonko1/demoPrediction/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T05:08:39.794Z","hash":"000102e4b0eefd3f5829faea3ed868817a981696e4ff408f8d78ff0ccac4762c","originalBytes":9579,"storedBytes":9579,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["npm","run","validate","house","data","scenario","build","map","presidential","senate","state","election","assumptions","controls","historical","local","start","baseline","baselines","model","national","stress","export","margin","next.js","open","static","swing","analysis","available","district","docs","geometry","launch","out","save","sensitivity","source","src","test","url","workspaces","accuracy","bash","before","carlo","congressional-d